  "description": "Aeras 24 starts with a Ventus Series hybrid frame that features Rider Optimized Geometry specifically designed to assure a proper and comfortable fit for smaller riders and adapted to fit a 24\" wheel. All Ventus Series models are ideally suited to a wide range of uses but for kids it comes down to fun, fitness, school, and good old \"just hanging\" around the neighborhood. Aeras 24 uses a rigid steel fork with disc mounts to increase pedal efficiency by preventing energy loss associated with excess fork movement. Aeras 24 comes complete with a 1x8 speed drive train to keep things simple and light while still remaining versatile. Its wheelset is made from Pivit alloy disc hubs laced to durable 24\" alloy double wall rims and all weather stopping is made possible thanks to a pair of Promax mechanical disc brakes.\nHaro Ventus Juvenile Sport Hybrid frame with Rider Optimized Geometry, mechanically-shaped alloy tubing, internal cable routing and chainstay disc brake mount\nHaro Ventus steel fork with disc brake mounts\nAlloy 3-pc crankset, 32t chainring with sealed cartridge BB\nShimano Altus rear derailleur\nShimano Altus 8-spd speed Rapidfire Plus rear shifter\nWide-ratio Shimano HG-200 12-32 8 speed cassette\nPivit disc brake hubs and lightweight double wall rims\nSize-specific saddle & brake levers\nNew Pivit alloy 9* sweep flattop bar, and forged stem\nPromax DK-300 mechanical disc brakes",
